This exam is scenario-grounded, not a trivia quiz about API parameter names. Every real
item drops the candidate into a realistic production situation (an agent misbehaving, a
tool call failing, a context window filling up, a team debating an architecture) and asks
them to make the right architectural call. Match that style exactly:

- Write a short scenario (2-5 sentences) with concrete, specific detail (not generic filler).
- Ask one question anchored to that scenario.
- Provide 4-6 answer choices. Distractors must be plausible - things a rushed or
under-informed candidate would pick - not obviously wrong filler.
- State whether the candidate should "Select one answer." or "Select N answers." and make
`correct_indices` match that count exactly.
- Tag difficulty (easy/medium/hard) honestly - most real items are medium.
- In `grounding_notes`, write the actual reasoning: why the correct answer(s) are right and
why each distractor is wrong. This is for later use in generating explanations - be specific
and technically accurate, don't hand-wave.

Do not repeat the same scenario premise across items. Vary the situations.